From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuttlely vendor <vendor@cuttlely.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlely: unused runtime dependencies

What: pyproject.toml drops tenacity, jinja2, watchfiles and resvg-py from the core dependency list, and uv.lock is relocked for Python 3.14 with the pinned uv. jinja2 stays on the kittentts extra and watchfiles stays on the modal extra. It also raises the mcp pin from 2.0.0 to 2.2.0 in the mcp and computer-use extras and the dev group, and uv.lock moves mcp and mcp-types to 2.2.0. Why: a harness run does not import those four, so the image install should not pull them from the locked set. mcp 2.2.0 fixes GHSA-84m7-p3x7-pcfv (unbounded session accumulation in the StreamableHTTP transport). The upstream pin is exact, so the raise edits pyproject.toml, and this is the last patch that edits that file. The other security pins stay in the previous patch. Drop the mcp raise once upstream pins 2.2.0 or later.
---
 pyproject.toml |  19 +++-------
 uv.lock        | 100 +++++--------------------------------------------
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 105 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index effbad28b1548e7255e948eae4c8bf1780bc5278..6402f3ae4e540df55fb0cdbb6fde79f2384cd98d 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -50,12 +50,10 @@ dependencies = [
   "fire==0.7.1; python_version >= '3.14'",
